PROMPT HISTORY - post-hackathon cleanup of GenoPheno_Embedding_Validator
=========================================================================

Prompt 1 - Split the repo into two pipelines, clean up part 1, test on CPU
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Request (paraphrased): The project is a pipeline in two parts: (1) haplograph -> embeddings ->
fine-tuning Evo 2, and (2) proteomics -> embeddings -> fine-tuning Evo 2. Put each part's scripts
and folders in its own subdirectory and organize the README in two parts, changing only formatting
(no content removed or modified) and adding information about code the README does not mention.
Do not modify part 2 code; clean up only part 1 with the hackathon-cleanup skill. For part 1: add
download instructions to the README and a download_haplograph.py script (genome-wide or per
chromosome) that produces the training and test sets for fine-tuning/testing Evo 2; remove
2_ancestry_labels.py; merge step 3 with the RAPIDS step 3 (node2vec, xgboost and gnn, no ancestry
labels); merge step 4 with the BioNeMo step 4 behind a --bionemo flag, taking step 3's embeddings;
make step 5 a validator of the fine-tuned Evo 2 on the test set; remove scratch_code/; move
How_to_use_rapids into README or DOCUMENTATION; keep and fix install_evo2.sh and
validation_tasks.txt; test the pipeline on CPU (no GPU here) but make it run on GPU; include RAPIDS,
CuPy, BioNeMo and Nemotron if possible; document installation and running in DOCUMENTATION.md.

Decisions confirmed with the user:
  - XGBoost (step 3) target without labels: the node's haploblock region (genomic bins).
  - 4b_finetune_evo2_hash.py: kept as an optional extra in part 1.
  - data/ and clinical_dashboard/ go to part 2; example_test_run/ (ancestry checkpoint) deleted.
  - Nemotron: optional plain-language summary of the step-5 report (--nemotron-summary).

